      "path": "content/Stickyickistan.md",
      "ok": true,
      "totalLines": 73,
      "returnedRange": {
        "startLine": 55,
        "endLine": 73
      },
      "hasMoreBelow": false,
      "nextStartLine": null,
      "content": "55|When [[Duke Doobius Highblade]] died, his human heirs inherited the family’s formal authority and attempted to preserve the old order. The Twothirdlings, who heavily outnumbered the Elyrian population around Doobius House, rejected that arrangement. Led by [[Jimmyjock Labingi]], the disinherited duke’s half-breed Twothirdling son, they seized the estate and surrounding settlement, declaring that Doobius House belonged to the people who had made it livable and defended it.\n56|\n57|Jimmyjock formed a provisional government and began negotiations with the Elyrian nobility of [[Nevercough City]]. The negotiations quickly broke down. The nobles refused to recognize the Twothirdlings’ claim to the settlement, while Jimmyjock refused to surrender the land or accept an arrangement that would leave his mother’s people subject to the family that had rejected him.\n58|\n59|## The [[Arcane Civil War]]\n60|\n61|The dispute over Doobius House became one of the first major armed conflicts between the Elyrian settlers and the native resistance. House Highblade forces attempted to retake the estate and secure the frontier road, while volunteers from Doobius House fortified the settlement and used the surrounding wilderness as a weapon.\n62|\n63|The resulting skirmishes spread into what is now known as the [[Grim Forest]]. Doobius House’s militia was badly outnumbered, but its fighters knew the terrain intimately. They used brutal guerrilla tactics, striking at night, cutting supply lines, sabotaging war machines, and disappearing into the forest before the larger Elyrian forces could respond. Old arcane ballistae, nature-infused war machines, trained beasts, and improvised traps allowed the resistance to ambush troops who expected a quick victory.\n64|\n65|The fighting around Doobius House became entangled with the wider power struggles among the [[Four Founding Houses]]. Rival nobles supported, supplied, or undermined the campaign according to their own interests. Industrial sabotage, magical duels, and full-scale battles tore the emerging nation apart, with factions summoning fiends, creating unstable war golems, and using necromantic plagues to gain the upper hand. These conflicts eventually widened into the [[Arcane Civil War]].\n66|\n67|As the cost of the campaign mounted, the nobles of Nevercough City grew weary of trying to dominate a settlement that refused to surrender. The resistance had demonstrated that Doobius House could not be conquered cheaply, while continued warfare threatened trade routes and the stability of the coastal settlements.\n68|\n69|Jimmyjock used his knowledge of Elyrian law and military practice, combined with the indigenous values of his mother’s people, to negotiate a settlement. The final agreement recognized the Twothirdlings’ right to govern Doobius House, while allowing Elyrian families and institutions to remain in the region under negotiated protections. The settlement did not erase the violence or the unequal power that produced it, but it prevented House Highblade from reclaiming the town by force.\n70|\n71|Doobius House remained an autonomous and heavily armed frontier community for generations. Its workshops continued producing arcane ballistae and nature-infused war machines, officially for defense against the dangers of [[The Outback]], but also as a reminder that the town’s independence had been won through resistance. Jimmyjock’s songs preserved the memory of the conflict, while Elyrian histories recast him as a rebel and thief of noble property.\n72|\n73|In the aftermath of the [[Emerald Blight]] and the destruction of [[Spliffholm]], the surviving settlements eventually united into the city-state of Stickyickistan. Doobius House lost much of its former independence as roads, bureaucracy, and urban expansion absorbed the frontier town into the wider state. Even so, the resistance remains central to its identity: the place where the Twothirdlings first proved that the Elyrian settlements could be challenged, and where Jimmyjock Labingi turned a disputed inheritance into a homeland.",
